    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** serving as our undisputed anchor. His 85.83 efficiency score is bolstered by an elite 0.423 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Miller, B, making him a must-start despite the park factors. Close behind him, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides significant upside at a 79.70 score; given our organizational focus on the scarcest category, his speed profile against a pitcher like Ritchie\u2014who historically struggles to suppress baserunners\u2014makes him our highest-ceiling play for stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** (62.66) and **Luke Raley** (62.37) benefit from wind-out conditions and favorable platoon alignments, respectively, allowing us to project a high floor for power production across the outfield.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the MI slot, where **Caleb Durbin** narrowly earned the start over our other depth pieces. While his 57.80 score is tempered by a lineup position at #9, the environmental conditions\u2014specifically the wind blowing out\u2014tipped the scales in his favor, as he remains one of our primary threats to steal a base if he can reach. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** presents the most risk in the lineup today; his 40.80 score is hovering just above the \"marginal\" threshold, suppressed by a negative platoon split against Scott. We are monitoring this closely, as **Gary Sanchez** or **Josh Smith** remain ready should any late-inning defensive switches be required. We remain cautious regarding the top of the order, as **Junior Caminero** faces a stiff test against Cease; however, his strong lineup placement at #2 provides enough insulation to keep him firmly in the mix.",
